hadiths[165]{hadithnumber,text}:
"10231","Abu Dawud told us, he said: Muhammad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Issa bin Abi Razin al-Thumali al-Homsi told us, on the authority of Luqman bin Amir On the authority of Awasat Al-Bajli, he heard Abu Bakr giving a sermon on the pulpit, and he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, giving a sermon. On the pulpit the first year in this position of mine, and his eyes shed tears, when he mentioned the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Ask God for well-being. For, after certainty, no servant has been given anything better than well-being.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10232","Yahya bin Uthman told us, he said: Omar bin Abdul Wahid told us, he said: Abdul Rahman bin Yazid bin Jabir told us, he said: Suleiman bin Amer told me, he said: I heard Awat al-Bajli, on the pulpit of Homs, saying: I heard Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, saying: A messenger has risen among us. The first year, may God bless him and grant him peace, for the sake of my father and my mother, then he was choked by grief, then he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, rose among us. The first year he greeted my mother and father and said: “Ask God for well-being, for no servant has been given anything better after certainty than well-being.”"
"10233","Mahmoud bin Khalid told me, he said: Al-Walid told us, he said: Ibn Jabir told us, he said: Sulaym bin Amir told me, he said: I heard the middle Al-Bajli, saying: I heard Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, saying: The Messenger of God rose among us the first year, so my father and my mother were sacrificed for him, then The lesson choked him, then he came back and said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace in the first year, saying: “Ask God for forgiveness and well-being.” And well-being, for no servant has been given better after certainty than well-being.”"
"10234","Ali bin Al-Hussein told us, he said: Umayyah bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Yazid bin Khumayr, on the authority of Sulaym bin Amir, on the authority of Al-Bajli was in the middle and said: Abu Bakr addressed us, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood in my place this year for the first year, then he moved on. Then he said: “Ask God for well-being, for no one has been given after certainty better than well-being. Do not envy one another, do not separate one another, and do not Compete, and be brothers as God has commanded you.”"
"10235","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman told us, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Salih, on the authority of Sulaym, on the authority of Awsat al-Bajli, he said: I came to Medina a year after the death of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I saw Abu Bakr addressing the people. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, rose among us. May God bless him and grant him peace in the first year, and he was repeatedly stifled by grief, then he said: “O people, ask God for well-being, for no one has been given protection yet.” Certainty is like well-being, and there is nothing more severe than doubt after disbelief, and you must be honest, for it guides to righteousness, and they will both be in Paradise, and beware of you. And lying, for it leads to immorality, and they will both be in Hell.”"
"10236","Amr bin Othman told me, he said: My father told us, he said: Abu Khalid Al-Mahrami Muhammad bin Omar, his name told us, on the authority of Thabit bin Saad Al-Ta’i, on the authority of Jubayr bin Nufayr, who said: Abu Bakr stood up and mentioned the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he cried, then he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, May God bless him and grant him peace. He stood in my position this first year and said: “O people, ask God for well-being three times, for no one has been given the like of well-being.” \with certainty\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"10237","Ishaq bin Mansour told us, on the authority of Ahmad bin Hanbal, he said: Bahz bin Asad told us, he said: Sulaym bin Hayyan told us, he said: I heard Qatada, on the authority of Humaid bin Abdul Rahman, that Omar said: Abu Bakr addressed us, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He stood up among us in the first year and said: “Nothing has been divided among the people better than well-being after certainty. Indeed, honesty and righteousness in Paradise, but lies and immorality are in Hell.”"
"10238","Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, he said: Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, rose among us the first year I rose among you. He said: “The people have not been given anything better than forgiveness.” And wellness, so ask God for them.” And Muhammad bin Rafi’ informed us, he said: Husayn bin Ali informed us, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Salih, he said: Abu Bakr on the pulpit, something like that. He told us about it twice, once like this, and once like that. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10239","Muhammad bin Ali bin Al-Hasan bin Shaqiq told us, on the authority of his father’s hadith, he said: Abu Hamza told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Some of the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Abu Bakr rose in the year he was appointed caliph, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, rose among us. He said: “O people, ask God for well-being, for He has not given anyone anything. What is better than well-being is not certainty.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10240","Muhammad bin Abdullah told us, he said: Yahya told us, meaning the son of Adam, he said: Ibn al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Yazid bin Jabir, on the authority of Al-Qasim Abi Abdul Rahman, said: I heard Uqba bin Amir, saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited He recited the two Mu’awwidhas in prayer, and he said to me: “Recite them whenever you sleep, and whenever you get up.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10241","Qutaibah bin Sa’id informed us, saying: Ya’qub told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Sa’id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “If one of you gets up from his bed and then comes back, let him shake it off with a piece of his clothes, for he does not know what was left in it.” After him, then when he lies down, let him say: In your name I have placed my side, and in you I raise it up. O God, if I hold my soul, forgive it, and if You sent it, so protect it with what You protect the righteous among Your servants.”"
"10242","I am Ali bin Hajar, Ismail told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abdullah bin Abdul Qari, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib, He said: I stayed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, one night, and I used to hear him say: Oh God, I seek refuge in Your forgiveness from Your punishment, I seek refuge in Your pleasure from Your anger, and I seek refuge in You from You. Oh God, I cannot praise You, even if I was careful, but you are just as you praised yourself.” Muhammad bin Abdul Rahim Al-Barqi told us, he said: Yahya bin Hassan told us, he said: Ismail bin Ja’far told us, he said: he told us Yazid bin Khusaifa, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdul Qari, on the authority of Ali, and the like. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10243","Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, he said: Bakr, meaning Ibn Mudar, informed us, on the authority of Ibn al-Hadi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Khabab, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri said that he heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “If one of you sees a vision and loves it, then it is from God. Let him praise God for it, and speak of it, and if he sees anything other than that which he dislikes, then it is from Satan, so let him seek refuge in God. Of its evil, and do not mention it to anyone, for it will not harm him.”"
"10244","Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Al-Hakam told us, he said: Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: I heard Abd Rabbuh Ibn Saeed narrates, on the authority of Abu Salamah, he said: If I were to see the dream and it would make me sick, then I went to see Abu Qatada. He said: I was to see the dream. It made me sick until I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “If one of you sees something that he loves, he should not tell it to anyone except those he loves. If he sees something that he dislikes, let him spit on his left three times, and let him seek refuge in God from the accursed Satan and its evil three times, and do not speak of it to anyone. It will not harm him.” Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, saying: Ubayd Allah told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Salamah, he said : The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever sees a vision will admire it.” Sent (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10245","Ishaq bin Mansour told us, he said: Abu Al-Mughirah told us, he said: Al-Awza’i told us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Qatada, on the authority of his father: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A good dream is from God, and a dream is from Satan. If one of you dreams a dream If he fears it, let him spit on his left side three times, and let him seek refuge in God from Satan, for it will not harm him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10246","Ishaq bin Mansour informed us, he said: Muhammad bin Kathir informed us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Qatada, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A good vision is good news from God, and a dream is from Satan. So if one of you dreams a dream He hates it, so let him spit on his left three times, and let him seek refuge in God from Satan, for it will not harm him.” Abu Salamah said: If the vision was to make me sleep until I heard the hadith of Abu Qatada (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10247","Mahmoud bin Khalid told us, he said: Al-Walid told us, he said: Abu Amr told us, he said: Yahya bin Abi Kathir told us, he said: Abdullah bin Abi Qatada told me, on the authority of his father: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A good vision is from God, and a dream is from Satan, so if one of you dreams a dream that he fears, let him spit to his left, and seek refuge in God from Satan, for it will not harm him,” he said. Yahya: Then Abu Salama told me, he said: If I dream a dream, I fear him until he makes me lie down. So I met Abu Qatada and he told me about this."
"10248","Ishaq bin Mansour told us, he said: Bishr bin Shuaib told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Abu Salamah told me, Abu Qatada said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “A good vision is from God, and a dream is from Satan. “If one of you dreams a dream that he hates, let him spit on his left three times, and seek refuge in God from it, for it will not harm him.”"
"10249","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Qatada On the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “The vision is from God, and the dream is from Satan. If one of you sees something that he hates, Let him blow on his left three times, and let him seek refuge in God from its evil, for it will not harm him.”"
"10250","Ali bin Harb told us, he said: Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Abu Salamah, he said: I heard Abu Qatada saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The vision is from God, and the dream is from Satan, so if one of you sees something that he hates, let him avoid it.” to his left hand three times, then to seek refuge from its evil, for it will not harm him.”"
"10251","Ali bin Harb told us again, he said: Ibn Fudayl told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The vision is from God, and the dream is from Satan, so whoever sees any of that will hate it.” So let him seek refuge in God from it, and spit out three things to his left, and do not mention them to anyone, for that will not harm him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10252","Ali bin Harb told us again, he said: Ibn Fudayl told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A vision is based on three things: good news from God, sorrow from Satan, and something that happens.” with it when a person sees it in his dream.”"
"10253","Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, And he said: “A good vision is one of forty-six parts of prophecy.” And he said: “A good vision is from God, and a dream is from Satan, if one of you dreams a dream that he fears, let him spit on his left three times, and seek refuge in God from his evil, for he will never \harm him\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"10254","Abu Salih al-Makki told us, he said: Fudayl, meaning Ibn Iyadh, told us, on the authority of al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you sees in his dream something that he dislikes, let him blow three blows on his left. And let him seek refuge in God from what he saw.”"
"10255","Muhammad bin Ali bin Al-Hasan bin Shaqiq told us, he said: I heard my father, he said: Abu Hamza told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Salih, On the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Umm Salamah, on the authority of the Prophet, she said: “If a man sees in his dream something that he dislikes, let him spit to his left three times, and seek refuge in By God from Satan.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10256","Ahmad bin Saeed told me, he said: Al-Ala’ bin Usaym told us, he said: Abu Zubayd told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Abu Salih, On the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Umm Salamah, she said: “If one of you sees a vision that he dislikes, let him spit to his left, then seek refuge from Satan.”"
"10257","Muhammad bin Al-Ala informed us in his hadith, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Ayyash, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Abu Salih, he said: Abu Hurairah said: “ A good vision is good news from God, and these are the ones that bring good tidings. So whoever among you sees a vision that displeases him, let him not tell it to anyone, and let him shun. three times to his left, for it will not harm him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10258","Ahmad bin Bakkar told me, he said: Muhammad, who is Ibn Salamah, told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Salamah Ibn Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Abu Qatada, said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “A vision is in three stages: some of them are A man tells himself about it, but it is nothing, and some of it is from Satan and it will not harm him, and some of it is a vision from God, so if If one of you sees something that he likes, let him present it to someone who has a sound opinion. Let him interpret it well and say good things, for the vision of a righteous servant is part of Of forty-six parts of prophecy.” Awf bin Malik said: By God, O Messenger of God, if it were one of the number of pebbles, it would be many. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10259","Ahmad bin Abi Ubayd Allah told us, he said: Yazid told us, and he is Ibn Zuray’, he said: Sa’id told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There are three types of visions: a true vision, a vision with which a man tells himself, And a vision of sorrow from Satan, so whoever sees something that he dislikes, let him stand up and pray.”"
"10260","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said “If one of you sees a vision that he dislikes, let him spit on his left three times, and seek refuge in God from Satan, and turn away from his side.” which was upon him\""
10261"""
"10261","Qutaybah ibn Sa'id informed us, saying: Al-Layth narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) that he said to a Bedouin who came to him: ""I dreamed that my head was cut off, and I was following it."" The Prophet (ﷺ) rebuked him and said: ""Do not inform (others) of the devil's play with you in your sleep."""
"10262","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Abu Ahmad Al-Zubayri told us, he said: Omar bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Abi Rabah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah said: A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: I saw my head being hit in a dream and I saw him threatening it? He laughed and said: “Satan approaches one of you and makes him disgraceful, then he goes out in the morning and tells the people about it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10263","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Yazid told us, meaning Ibn Al-Miqdam bin Shurayh bin Hani, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his father Shurayh, Aisha told him that when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw a cloud approaching from one of the horizons, he would leave whatever was in it. And if he is in prayer until he faces it, he says: “O God, we seek refuge in You from the evil with which we have been sent.” And if it rains, he says: “O God, leave us alone.” Beneficial, O God, a beneficial rain, and if God reveals it and does not rain, praise be to God for that.”"
"10264","Ibrahim bin Muhammad al-Taymi al-Qadi informed us, saying: Yahya told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, who said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw something appearing on one of the horizons of the sky, he would abandon his work, even if he was in prayer. God revealed it, he praised God, and if it rained, he said: “Oh God, let go.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10265","Amr bin Sawad bin Al-Aswad told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Yunus told us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw rain, he would say: “O God, make it a rain of mercy and do not make it a rain of torment.”"
"10266","Ali bin Khashram told us, he said: Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, on the authority of Aisha, When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw rain, he would say: “Oh God, grant us a pleasant rain.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10267","Mahmoud bin Khalid told me, he said: Al-Walid told us, on the authority of Abu Amr, he said: Nafi’ told me, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, on the authority of Aisha She said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw rain, he would say: “O God, make it a pleasant rain.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10268","Mahmoud bin Khalid told us, he said: Omar told me, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, he said: A man told me, on the authority of Nafi’, that Al-Qasim bin Muhammad He told him, on the authority of Aisha, that whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw rain, he would say: “Oh God, make it a pleasant rain.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10269","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Yahya bin Abdullah bin Al-Dahhak told us, he said: Al-Awza’i told us, he said: Muhammad told me Ibn al-Walid, on the authority of Nafi’, that al-Qasim ibn Muhammad told him, on the authority of Aisha, that whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw rain, he said: “Oh God, make it a happy rain.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10270","Abdah bin Abd al-Rahim al-Marwazi informed me, he said: Salama bin Sulayman informed us, he said: Ibn al-Mubarak informed us, he said: I am Ubaid. Allah bin Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Aisha, that when the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw rain, he would say: “Oh God, grant us rain.” \Congratulations\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"10271","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, he said: Nafi’ told me, on the authority of Al-Qasim, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace When he saw rain, he, peace and blessings of God be upon him, would say: “Oh God, have a good rain.”"
"10272","Amr ibn Sawad ibn al-Aswad ibn Amr informed us, saying: I am Ibn Wahb. He said: Yunus informed us, on the authority of al-Zuhri, he said: He informed me. Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “God Almighty said: What I have bestowed upon My servants of A blessing, except that a party of them became disbelievers in it, saying: The star, and by the star.”"
"10273","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Salih bin Kaysan, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Zayd bin Khalid He said: It rained on the people during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “Did you not hear what your Lord Almighty said tonight?” He said: “What I have bestowed a blessing upon My servants, except that a group of them became disbelievers therein, saying: We rained under such-and-such a storm. But as for whoever believes in Me, And whoever praises Me for giving me water, that is the one who believed in Me, but disbelieved in the star. And whoever says: We gave rain under such-and-such a storm, that is the one who disbelieved in Me and believed. \By the planet\"""""
"10274","Muhammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Ibn al-Qasim told us, on the authority of Malik, he said: Salih bin Kaysan told me, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah On the authority of Zaid bin Khalid Al-Juhani, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed the morning prayer in Medina in the wake of a night sky. When he left, he went to the people and said: “Do you know what your Lord, the Mighty and Majestic, said?” They said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: “He said: It was the morning of My servant is a believer, but as for whoever says: We have rained by the grace and mercy of God, he is a believer in Me, a disbeliever in the planet. As for whoever says: Our rain According to such-and-such, he is a disbeliever in Me, a believer in the star.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10275","Abu Dawud Suleiman bin Saif told us, he said: Affan bin Muslim told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Amr bin Muslim told us A dinar, on the authority of Attab, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If God withheld the drop from My nation for ten years, then He sent down water, and a group of my nation became disbelievers among it, saying: It is the building of glory.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Al-Majdhid Al-Shara’i"
"10276","Muhammad bin Ali bin Harb Al-Maruzi told us, he said: Sayyar bin Hatim told us, he said: Abdul-Wahid bin Ziyad told us, on the authority of Abu Matar, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, heard thunder and lightning, he would say: “Oh God, do not kill us.” anger, and do not kill us out of vengeance and treat us well before that.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10277","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, saying: Abd al-Wahid bin Ziyad told us, on the authority of al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Matar, that he heard Salim bin Abd God speaks, on the authority of his father, who said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, heard thunder and lightning, he would say: “Oh God, do not kill us.” with Your wrath, and do not destroy us with Your torment, and protect us before that.”"
"10278","Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Hakam told me, he said: Talq ibn al-Samh narrated to us, he said: Nafi’ ibn Yazid narrated to us, on the authority of Aqeel, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “The wind From the Spirit of God, it is sent with mercy, and it is sent with torment, so do not curse it, and say: O God, we ask You for its goodness, and we seek refuge in You from \Her evil\"""""
"10279","Othman bin Abdullah told me, he said: Muhammad bin Sulaiman told me, he said: Al-Hasan bin Ayan told me, he said: Omar bin Salem told us Al-Aftas, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Amr bin Sulaym Al-Zarqi, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: A wind blew and they attacked it, so the Prophet said, “Pray May God bless him and grant him peace: “Do not curse the wind, but ask God for its goodness, and seek refuge in Him from its evil.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10280","Yusuf bin Saeed told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ziyad told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, that he told him, he said Thabit bin Qais told me that Abu Hurairah said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “The wind comes from the Spirit of God. With mercy and it brings torment, so do not revile it, and ask God for its goodness, and seek refuge in Him from its evil.”"
"10281","Humayd bin Masada informed us, on the authority of Sufyan, who is Ibn Habib, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Thabit Al-Zarqi, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, the wind is from the Spirit of God, it brings mercy and punishment, so do not curse it. “And ask Him for its goodness, and seek refuge in Him from its evil.”"
"10282","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Asbat bin Muhammad told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ubayy ibn Ka’b, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Do not curse the wind, for if You see some of it that you dislike, so say: O God, we ask you for the good of this wind, the good of what is in it, and the good of what it was sent with, and we seek refuge in Protect you from the evil of this wind, and from the evil of what is in it, and from the evil of what it was sent with.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10283","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Ayyash Al-Raqqam Abu Al-Walid told us, he said: Muhammad bin Al-Fudayl told us. Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Habib bin Al-Shahid told us, and the wording for it, he said: Ibn Al-Fudayl told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Dhar, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abdul Rahman bin Abza, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ubayy bin Ka’b, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: “Do not curse the wind. If you see something that you dislike, say: O God, we ask You for the good of this wind and the good of what is in it. And the best of what you have been commanded to do, and we seek refuge in You from the evil of this wind, the evil of what is in it, and the evil of what you have been commanded to do.” Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told me, he said: Yahya bin Hammad told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ubayy ibn Ka`b, who said: “Do not curse the wind, for it is from the breath of The Most Gracious, the Almighty, the Most Gracious, the Most Gracious, the Most Gracious, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10284","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us, he said: Jarir informed us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Habib ibn Abi Thabit, on the authority of Dhar, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ubayy ibn Ka’b, he said: “Do not curse the wind, for it is from the soul of the Most Gracious, Blessed and Most High. But ask God for its goodness, and seek refuge from its evil.”"
"10285","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Sahl bin Hammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Dhar, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ubayy ibn Ka’b, who said: A wind arose and a man cursed it, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: He said: “Do not curse it, and ask God for its good, and the good that is in it, and the good with which it was sent, and seek refuge in God from its evil and the evil of what is in it. And the evil with which it was sent.” Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Dhar, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abdul Rahman bin Abza, On the authority of his father, on the authority of Ubayy ibn Ka’b, similar to it but not a chain of narrators, Ishaq ibn Mansour informed us, he said: Ibn Shumayl narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah told us, on the authority of Habib, who said: I heard Dhar, on the authority of Ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, on the authority of his father, that the wind blew on My father’s era, and the like (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10286","Ahmad ibn Amr ibn al-Sarh informed us, saying: Ibn Wahb informed us, saying: I heard Ibn Jurayj speaking, on the authority of Ata’ ibn Abi Rabah, On the authority of Aisha, she said: When the wind blew, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say: “O God, I ask You for the best of it, and the best with which you were sent.” “And I seek refuge in You from its evil, the evil of what is in it, and the evil of what it was sent with.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10287","Ishaq bin Mansour told us, he said: Othman bin Omar told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj told us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Aisha, “that the Messenger God, may God bless him and grant him peace, whenever he saw a wind, he would ask God for the best of it, the good of it, and the good of what it was sent with, and he would seek refuge in God from “The evil of it, and the evil of what is in it, and of what it was sent with.”"
"10288","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Khaled, who is Ibn Yazid, on the authority of Saeed, who is Ibn Abi Hilal, on the authority of Saeed. Ibn Ziyad, on the authority of Jabir Ibn Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O people of Islam, Reduce the going out after the man has calmed down, for God has animals that He spreads across the earth, so whoever hears the barking of a dog, or the braying of a donkey, let him seek refuge. God from Satan, for they see what you do not see.”"
"10289","Wahb bin Bayan told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Al-Layth bin Sa’d and Sa’id bin Abi Ayyub told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Rabia, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If you hear a roosters crow At night, it has seen an angel, so ask God for His bounty, and when you hear donkeys braying, it has seen a devil, so seek refuge in God. From Satan, the accursed.”"
"10290","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Rabi’ah, on the authority of Al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “If you hear a rooster crow, ask God for His bounty, for it has seen an angel, and if you hear a donkey braying... So seek refuge in God from Satan, for she saw Satan.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10291","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Musa bin Dawud told us, he said: Abdul Aziz bin Abi Salamah told us, on the authority of Salih bin Kaysan, On the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Zaid bin Khalid Al-Juhani, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not curse the rooster, for it He calls to prayer.” Zuhair bin Muhammad disagreed with him and sent the hadith (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10292","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Abu Amir, he said: Zuhair told us, on the authority of Salih bin Kaysan, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, that the rooster crowed in the presence of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and a man from the Ansar cursed him and said: “Do not curse the rooster, for he calls for \Prayer\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"10293","Ali bin Hajar informed us, saying: Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman bin Yazid bin Jabir and Al-Walid bin Muslim told us, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman bin Yazid, on the authority of Yahya bin Jabir Al-Tai, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Jubayr bin Nufayr Al-Hadrami, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Nawwas Ibn Samaan said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, mentioned the Antichrist one morning, and he lowered and raised it to the point that we thought he was in a group of palm trees. He said: “I fear for you other than the Antichrist. If he emerges while I am among you, then we will plead with him rather than you. If he emerges while I am not among you, then a person will be a pilgrim.” Himself, and God is my successor over every Muslim, he is a young man, with set eyes, as if he resembles Abd al-Uzza ibn Qattan. If someone among you sees him, let him recite the openings of Surah Ashab al-Kahf.”"
"10294","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: Qatada told me, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Al-Ja’d, on the authority of Ma’dan, on the authority of Thawban, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever recites the last ten days of Surah Al-Kahf, he will A protection for him from the Antichrist.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10295","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Muhammad bin Jaafar told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Salim bin Abi al-Ja’d, On the authority of Maadan, on the authority of Abu al-Darda’, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Whoever recites ten verses from the Cave will be protected from the temptation of the Antichrist.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10296","Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, he said: Shu’bah told me, on the authority of Qatada, he said: I heard Salim bin Abi Al-Ja’d. He narrates, on the authority of Ma’dan, on the authority of Abu Darda’, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “Whoever recites the last ten days of the Cave will be protected from temptation.” Antichrist (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10297","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Affan told us, he said: Hammam told us, he said: Qatadah used to narrate it to us, Salim bin told us. Abu al-Ja`d, on the authority of the hadith of Ma`dan ibn Abi Talha, on the authority of Abu al-Darda`, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “Whoever memorizes ten Verses from the beginning of Surah Al-Kahf: “He will be protected from the temptation of the Antichrist.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10298","Yahya bin Muhammad bin Al-Sakan Al-Basri told us, he said: Yahya bin Kathir Abu Ghassan told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: Abu Hashim told us, on the authority of Abu Majliz, on the authority of Qays ibn Abbad, on the authority of Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, that the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said “Whoever recites Surah Al-Kahf as it was revealed, it will be a light for him from his place of residence to Mecca, and whoever recites ten verses from the end, the Antichrist will emerge.” He was not given authority over him.” Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Hashim, he said: I heard Abu Majliz narrating, On the authority of Qays ibn Ubbad, on the authority of Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, something similar but did not narrate it, and he said: “From where he recites it to Mecca,” and he said: “Whoever recites \the end of the cave\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"10299","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Hashim, on the authority of Abu Majlaz, on the authority of Qais Ibn Abbad, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, who said: “Whoever recites Surat Al-Kahf as it was revealed, then approaches the Antichrist, will not be overpowered by it, or will not “There will be a way for him, and whoever recites Surah Al-Kahf, there will be light for him from wherever he recited it, between him and Mecca.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10300","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Yazid told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “You must adhere to the deep snow, for the earth is folded at night, so when the ghouls attack you, call out the call to prayer.”"
"10301","Muhammad bin Yahya bin Abdullah Al-Naysaburi told us, he said: Saeed bin Abi Maryam told us, he said: Muhammad bin Jafar told us, he said: Yahya told us, meaning Ibn Saeed Al-Ansari, he said: Muhammad bin Abdul-Rahman bin As’ad bin Zurarah told me, on the authority of Ayyash Al-Salami, On the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, “The night of the jinn is that he was with Gabriel and I was with him,” so the Prophet made the prayer May God bless him and grant him peace, he was reciting, and the Ifrit began to approach and get closer, so Gabriel said to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Shall I not teach you some words?” You say them, and the ifrit is thrown onto its face, and its flame is extinguished. Say: I seek refuge in the Most Generous Face of God, and in His perfect words that do not Neither the righteous nor the immoral will pass over them, from the evil of what descends from the sky, and from what ascends therein, and from the evil of what He has spread on the earth, and from what comes out of it, and from The temptations of the night and the day, and from the evil of the Tariqs of the night and the day, there is only one Tariq that knocks with goodness, O Most Merciful. So the Ifrit bowed to his face, And his flame went out.” Malik bin Anas disagreed with him. Al-Harith bin Miskin told us of a reading of it while I was listening, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, he said: Malik told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, He said: He was taken captive by the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he saw a demon from the jinn seeking him with a flame of fire. Whenever the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, turned around He saw him, peace be upon him, and Gabriel, peace be upon him, said to him, and he narrated the hadith. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10302","Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Ubayd Allah told us, he said: Shuaib bin Harb told us, he said: Ismail bin Muslim told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Mutawakkil Al-Naji, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that he was collecting dates for charity, and he found the print of a palm as if it had been taken from it, So he mentioned that to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he said: “Do you want to take it? Say: Glory be to Him who has subjected you to Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him,” he said. Abu Hurairah: So I said, “If I saw it standing in my hands, I took it to take it to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Only I took it to the poor family of the jinn, and I will not return. He said: Then he returned, so I mentioned that to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “Do you want to “Do you take it?” I said: “Yes.” He said: “Say, ‘Glory be to Him who has subjugated you to Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace.’” So I said, “So I am with him.” So I would take him to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he promised me that he would not come back, so I left him. Then he returned, so I mentioned him to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said : Do you want to take it? So I said: Yes, and he said: “Say: Glory be to Him who has subjected you to Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace.” So I said: When I was with him, I said: You made a promise to me, but you lied. I promised that I would take you to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Leave me and I will teach you some words. If you say them, no male or female will approach you. A female of the jinn, so I said: What are these words? He said: I recite the Throne Verse every morning and evening. Abu Hurairah said: So I left. On his authority, I mentioned that to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “Did you not know that it was like that?” \ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"10303","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told us, he said: Othman bin Al-Haytham told us, he said: Awf told us, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entrusted me with keeping the zakat of Ramadan. Then a man came to me seeking some food, so I took it and said: I will take you to The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I am in need, I have children, and I am in great need, so I left him, and when I woke up, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said May God bless him and grant him peace: “O Abu Hurairah, what did your prisoner do yesterday?” I said: O Messenger of God, he complained of a dire need for his family, so I had mercy on him and left. On his way, he said: “But he has lied to you, and he will return.” So I knew that he would return to what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He will return. I noticed him and he came looking for food, so I said: I will take you to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Leave me alone, for I am in need and have children and no children. I returned, and I had mercy on him and released him on his way. In the morning, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O Abu Hurairah, what did your prisoner do yesterday?” ? Then he came asking for some food, so I took it and said: I will present you to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. This is the last three times you have claimed that you did not You come back and then come back. He said: He said: Let me teach you words with which God will benefit you. I said: What are they? He said: When you go to bed, recite the verse of the Throne, “Allah, there is no god but He, the Ever-Living, the Ever-Subsisting,” until you complete the verse, for He will not be lost to you. From God is a protector, and no devil will come near you until morning. So I did in the morning, and the Messenger of God said to me: “What did your prisoner do yesterday?” I said: O Messenger of God. God, he claimed that he was teaching me words that God would benefit me with, so I let him go. He said: “What are they?” He said to me: If you go to bed, recite a verse. The Throne from the beginning until you finish it. God, there is no god but He, the Ever-Living, the Ever-Subsisting. Satan until morning, and they were the most keen on goodness, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “But it is a lie and he has told you the truth. You know who Have you been speaking for three days, O Abu Hurairah?” I said: “No.” He said: “That Satan.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10304","Abdul Hamid bin Saeed told us, he said: Mubashir told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, he said: Yahya bin Abi Kathir told us, he said: he told me Ibn Ubayy said that his father told him that they had a grove with dates in it, and Ubayy was taking care of it, and he found it decreasing, so he guarded it, and then... He was an animal that looked like a pubescent boy. He said: So I greeted him and he returned my greeting, so I said: Who are you, a madman or a human? He said: A jinn. He said: So give me your hand. So he gave me his hand. Then, behold, the hand of a dog and the hair of a dog. He said: This is how the jinn was created. He said: You have known the jinn. None of them is stronger than me. My father said to him: What made you do what you did? He said: We have heard that you are a man who loves charity, so we would like to take a share of your food. My father said: What is the one who will give us a reward from among you? He said: This verse is the verse of the Throne. Then tomorrow he went to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and told him, and he said: “The evil one has spoken the truth.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10305","Abu Dawud told us, he said: Muadh bin Hani told us, he said: Harb bin Shaddad told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: he told us Al-Hadrami bin Lahiq Al-Tamimi, he said: Muhammad bin Ubayy bin Ka’b told me, he said: My grandfather had a jar of dates, so he started to find it was running low. So he guarded him one night, and he saw an animal that looked like a pubescent boy. He greeted him and he returned his greeting, and said: Who are you? A madman or a madman? Forget? He said: No, but a jinn. He said: Give me your hand. Then, behold, the hand of a dog and the hair of a dog. He said: This is how the jinn was created. He said: You have known the jinn, what is in them. A man stronger than me. He said: What is the matter with you? He said: I was informed that you are a man who loves charity, so we would like to share of your food. He said: What will reward us from you? He said: This is the verse that is in Surat Al-Baqarah: Allah, there is no god but He, the Ever-Living, the Ever-Subsisting. Neither sleep nor sleep overtakes Him, if you say it in the morning. You will be rewarded from us until the evening, and if you say it in the evening you will be rewarded from us until the morning. My father went back to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. So he told him his story, and said: “The evil one has spoken the truth.” Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Al-Hasan bin Musa told us, he said: Shayban told us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Al-Hadrami bin Lahiq, On the authority of Muhammad, he said: Ubayy ibn Ka’b was Muhammad’s grandfather. He said: “My father had a food jar, so he mentioned something similar to it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10306","Muhammad bin Nasr told us, he said: Ayoub, who is the son of Sulayman bin Bilal, told us, he said: Abu Bakr told me, on the authority of Sulayman, on the authority of Muhammad Bin Ajlan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “No If one of you places one of his legs on top of the other, sings, and leaves Surah Al-Baqarah to recite, then Satan flees from the House. Al-Baqarah will be recited therein. Indeed, the yellowest of houses is the hollow from the Book of God Almighty. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10307","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Salamah bin Kuhail, he said: I heard Abu Al-Ahwas, He said: Abdullah said: “Recite the Qur’an so that your young ones may be brought up in it, and your elders may not distance themselves from it, for Satan flees the house when he hears it being recited.”"
"10308","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Ya’qub, who is the son of Abd al-Rahman al-Zuhri, told us, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not make your homes graves, for Satan flees from the house in which Surah \The cow\"""""
"10309","Ibrahim bin Saeed Al-Jawhari told us, he said: Rayhan bin Saeed told us, he said: Abbad, who is Ibn Mansour, told us, on the authority of Ayoub, On the authority of Abu Qilaba, on the authority of Abu Salih. Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad bin Salam told us, saying: Rayhan told us, on the authority of Abbad, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalabah, that he claimed that It was narrated by Abu Saleh Al-Harithi, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Bashir, that the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said one day: “Indeed, God has written a book Two thousand years before He created the heavens and the earth, and Abraham said: Two thousand years. He is with Him on the throne, and that He was sent down from That book is two verses with which Surah Al-Baqarah was concluded, and Satan will not enter a house in which they were recited for three nights.” He was succeeded by Ash'ath ibn Abd al-Rahman. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10310","Amr bin Mansour told me, he said: Al-Hajjaj told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Ash’ath. And Ahmad bin Sulayman told us, he said: Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Al-Ash’ath bin Abd al-Rahman told us, On the authority of Abu Qalaba, on the authority of Abu al-Ash’ath al-San’ani, on the authority of al-Nu’man ibn Bashir, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Amr said: The Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “Indeed, God wrote a book two thousand years before He created the heavens and the earth, and He sent down from it two verses with which He concluded Surah Al-Baqarah, do not recite it in a house for three nights, lest Satan approach it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10311","Hilal bin Al-Ala told me, on the authority of his father, he said: Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Laila, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Abdul Rahman Ibn Abi Laila, on the authority of his father, said: I was sitting with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, when a man came to him and asked him about house snakes, and he said: “So If you see any of them in your dwellings, say: We admonish you by the covenant that Noah made upon you, and we adjure you by the covenant that he made upon you. Solomon, lest you harm us, but if they return, kill them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10312","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid al-Muqri informed us, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of Saifi Mawla Abu Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, in Medina, there are a group of jinn who have submitted to Islam, so if you see These Awamir are nothing, so call him out three times, but if he appears to you after that, kill him.” Brief. Al-Layth bin Sa’d and Yahya bin Sa’id disagreed with him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10313","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, he said: Shuaib bin Al-Layth told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Saifi Abu Sa’id Mawla Al-Ansar, on the authority of Abu Al-Sa’ib, that Abu Sa’id said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A group of the jinn in Medina converted to Islam. So if you see someone, warn him three times, then if it seems to you that you should kill him, then kill him after three times.”"
"10314","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, he said: Saifi told me, on the authority of Abu Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abu Saeed, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, in Medina, a group of jinn have converted to Islam, so whoever sees any of these signs... Let him call him to prayer three times, and if it appears to him yet, let him kill him, for he is a devil.”"
"10315","Al-Harith bin Miskin read about it while I was listening, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, who said: Malik told us, on the authority of Saifi, the client of Ibn Aflah, on the authority of Abu Al-Sa'ib, the client of Hisham bin Zahra, on the authority of Abu Sa'id Al-Khudri, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out to the trench, While he was there, a young man from the Ansar came who had recently made a wedding covenant, and said: O Messenger of God, permit me to make a covenant with my family. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave him permission, so the boy approached and saw his wife between the two doors, so he thrust his spear at her. To stab her, and she said: Do not be in a hurry to go in and see. So he entered and found a snake lying on his bed. When he saw it, he focused on it. His spear, then he set it up. Abu Sa’id said: Then the snake was disturbed at the tip of the spear until it died, and the boy fell down dead, and that was conveyed to the Messenger of God. God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Indeed, in Medina there are jinn who have converted to Islam, so if you see any of them, call it to it for three days, and if it appears Then kill him, for he is a devil.”"
"10316","Abdul Rahman bin Muhammad bin Salam told us, he said: Yazid told us, he said: Jarir bin Hazim told us, on the authority of Asma bin Ubaid, on the authority of A man from the city called Al-Sa’ib said: We were with Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri and he was sitting on his bed, so we saw him under his bed. A snake, so we said: O Abu Saeed, is this a snake under the bed? He said: Do not disturb them. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, these houses have signs, so if you see any of them, be disturbed by it.” Three, if he goes, otherwise kill him, for he is an infidel.” Brief (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10317","Muhammad bin Hisham Al-Sadusi told us, he said: Khalid bin Al-Harith told us, he said: Ash’ath told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that Ubayy said: I heard The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: “If one of you cherishes a goat of pre-Islamic times, give him his father’s share of it, and do not be embarrassed.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10318","Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Al-Mughirah told us, he said: Muawiyah told us, he is Ibn Hafs, he said: Al-Sari bin Yahya told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, On the authority of Utai, on the authority of Ubayy ibn Ka’b, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever you hear calling upon the pre-Islamic era, then support him.” his father, and do not deny it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10319","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khalid told us, he said: Awf told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Utai bin Damrah, he said: I witnessed it one day, meaning Ubayy ibn Ka’b, and behold, a man was being consoled by the condolences of pre-Islamic times, so he bit him with his father’s arrows and did not stab him, and it was as if The people denounced that of him, so he said: Do not blame me, for the Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to us: “Whom did you see being consoled? pre-Islamic times, so support him and do not neglect him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10320","Abd Al-Habbar bin Al-Ala’ bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: I memorized it from Amr, he said: I heard Jabir, he said We were with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a campaign, when a man from the immigrants kicked a man from the Ansar, and the Ansari said: Oh, the Ansar, and he said Al-Muhajiri: Oh, the Muhajireen. Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, heard about that, and he said: “What is the matter with the claim of pre-Islamic times?” They said: O Messenger of God, A man from among the immigrants stabbed a man from the Ansar, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Leave her, for she is stinking.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10321","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Hatim told us, on the authority of Yazid, who is Ibn Abi Ubaid, he said: I heard Salama bin Al-Akwa’, saying: I went out before the first call to prayer was given, and it was the vaccine of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with a monkey, and a boy of Abd al-Rahman bin Awf met me. He said: Did you take the vaccine from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? I said: Who took it? He said: Ghatafan, so I shouted three cries: O morning, so I heard what was between the two lions of the city, then I rushed on my face until I overtook them. They began to draw water, so I started shooting at them with my dart. I was an archer, and I said: I am Ibn al-Akwa’, and today is the day of infants. Then he mentioned Meaningful words, and he trembled until I recovered the vaccine from them and took thirty cloaks from them. He said: And the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came, and I said: “O Prophet of God, I have withheld water from the people, and they are thirsty, so send the hour.” He said: “O Ibn Al-Akwa’, you have taken possession of me, so I may prostrate myself.” Then we returned. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10322","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, and Yazid bin Zurai’ told us, they said: Al-Taymi and Mu’tamir told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abi Othman Al-Nahdi, on the authority of Qabisa bin Mukhariq and Zuhair bin Amr, who said: When it was revealed and warn your closest family, the Messenger of God concluded May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he went to a cleft of a mountain, set a stone on top of it, and then said: “O Banu Abd Manaf, I am only a warner. And your example is that of a man who saw the enemy and was afraid that they would outrun him to his family, so he started shouting: “O morning.” Muhammad ibn Abd told us. The highest, he said: Mu`tamar narrated to us, on the authority of his father, he said: Abu Uthman narrated to us, on the authority of Zuhayr bin Amr, on the authority of Qubaisa bin Mukhariq, he said: God Almighty revealed to the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and warn your closest family. He told us about the Prophet of God that he came upon a rock. From a mountain, and he made a stone on top of it, then he said: “O servant of his exile, O morning! Indeed, I am a warner.” He continued the hadith, and said at the end of it: Or as He said. Ya'qub bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Ibn Ulayya, on the authority of Sulayman, similarly, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to A mountain, and he made the highest of it a stone, then he said: “O Abd Manaf, I am a warner. My likeness and your likeness is like a man who saw the enemy and wanted to He was warning his family, but he was afraid that the enemy would overtake him, so he called out: “O morning.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10323","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: Muawiyah, who is the son of Hisham Al-Qassar, told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Saeed Ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: When the verse was revealed: And warn your closest kindred, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, rose at Safa and said: “And the two mornings”"
"10324","Abu Kurayb Muhammad ibn Al-Ala informed us, he said: Abu Muawiyah informed us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Amr ibn Murrah, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, ascended Safa one day and said: “O morning,” so she gathered to him. Quraysh and they said: What is the matter with you? He said: “Do you think that if I told you that the enemy would come to you in the morning or in the evening, would you believe me?” They said: Yes. He said: “For I am a warner.” A severe torment awaits you.” Then Abu Lahab said: “May curse be upon you. Is this for this you have called us all to?” Then God Almighty revealed: “May Abu Lahab’s hands rest.” And repent to the end (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10325","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Muqri informed us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Abdul-Malik bin Umair told us, on the authority of Raba’i On the authority of Hudhayfah, he said: I saw in my sleep as if a man from among the Jews was saying: You claim that we associate partners with God, and you associate others with Him. You say: What God willed and what Muhammad willed? So I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “As for me, I hated her for you. Say: God willing, and then you wish.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10326","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khalid told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mansour, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Yasar speaking, On the authority of Hudhayfah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not say: What God willed and so-and-so willed, but say: What God willed and then so-and-so willed.” \""
10327"""
"10327","Yusuf ibn 'Isa informed us, saying: Al-Fadl ibn Musa narrated to us, saying: Mis'ar informed us, from Ma'bad ibn Khalid, from 'Abdullah ibn Yasar, from Qutaylah, a woman from Juhaynah, that a Jew came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: ""You people associate partners (with Allah). You say: 'What Allah wills and what you will,' and you say: 'By the Ka'bah.'"" So the Prophet (ﷺ) commanded them that when they wished to swear an oath, they should say: ""By the Lord of the Ka'bah,"" and one of them should say: ""What Allah wills, then what you will."" Ahmad ibn Hafs informed us, saying: My father narrated to me, saying: Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to me, from al-Mughirah, from Ma'bad ibn Khalid, from Qutaylah, a woman from the female emigrants (muhajirat) of Juhaynah, who said: A Jewish woman entered upon 'A'ishah and said: ""You people associate partners (with Allah),"" and she related the hadith."
"10328","Muhammad bin Hatim Al-Muaddeb told us, he said: Al-Qasim bin Malik told us, he said: Al-Ajlah narrated to us, and he said after him: On the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, On the authority of Jabir, that a man came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and spoke to him, and he said: “What God wills,” meaning “as you will,” so he said: “Woe to you, by God, you have made me Just? Say: “Whatever God alone wills.” Issa bin Yunus disagreed with him (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10329","Ali bin Khashram told us, on the authority of Issa, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, on the authority of Yazid bin Al-Asam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that a man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted him and spoke to him about some matter. He said: “Whatever God wills and whatever you wish.” Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Have you made me a just person for God’s sake?” Say: “Whatever God wills.” \Alone\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"10330","Ahmad bin Bakkar told me, he said: Mukhlid told us, he said: Yunus, he is the son of Abi Ishaq, told us, on the authority of his father, he said: he told me Musaab bin Saad bin Abi Waqqas, on the authority of his father, said: I swore by Al-Lat and Al-Uzza, and my companions said to me: What an evil thing you said. I said in abandonment, so I came. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so I mentioned that to him, and he said: “Say, ‘There is no god but God. He alone has no partner. To Him belongs the dominion and to Him is praise.’” And He has power over all things, and spit out three things from your left hand, and seek refuge in God from Satan, and then do not repeat.”"
"10331","Abu Dawud told us, he said: Al-Hasan bin Muhammad told us, he said: Zuhayr told us, he said: Abu Ishaq told us, on the authority of Mus’ab bin Saad On the authority of his father, he said: We were mentioning some matter while I was fresh from pre-Islamic times, so I swore by Al-Lat and Al-Uzza, and the companions of the Messenger of God said to me: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: How evil is what you said. Go to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and tell him, for we have never seen you except that you disbelieved, so I met him. So I told him, and he said: “Say, ‘There is no god but God, alone, without any partner,’ three times, and seek refuge in God from Satan three times, and avoid \ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"10332","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Miskin bin Bukayr told us, he said: Al-Awza’i told us, he said: Al-Zuhri told me, on the authority of Humaid bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever among you swears and says in his oath: By Al-Lat and Al-Uzza, Let him say: There is no god but Allah, and whoever says to his friend: Come, I will gamble with you, let him give alms.”"
"10333","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala informed us, he said: Ibn Wahb informed me, he said: Yunus informed me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Humayd informed me Ibn Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever among you swears an oath and says in his oath: By Al-Lat and Al-Uzza, Let him say: There is no god but Allah, and whoever says to his friend: Come, I will gamble with you, let him give alms.”"
"10334","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Mansur, on the authority of Raba’i, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, on the authority of his father, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came and said: O Muhammad Abd al-Muttalib, he is better for your people than you. He feeds them with liver and hump, and you slaughter them. He said: So he said, “What God wills.” When he wanted to leave, he said: What should I say? He said: “Say: O God, protect me from the evil of my soul, and guide me to the right direction in my affairs.” So he set off, but he did not convert to Islam. Then he converted to Islam, so he said: O Messenger. By God, I came to you and said: Teach me, and you said: “Say: O God, protect me from the evil of myself, and guide me to the right path in my affairs.” So what should I say now when I have embraced Islam? He said: “Say: O God, protect me from the evil of my soul, and guide me to the right path in my affairs. O God, forgive me what I have done secretly and what I have declared, what I have done wrong and what I have done intentionally.” “And I did not know, nor did I know.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10335","Abu Ja`far ibn Abi Surayj al-Razi informed us. He said: Muhammad ibn Sa`id, who is the son of Sabiq al-Qazwini, informed me. He said: Amr told us, and he is Ibn Abi Qais, on the authority of Mansur, on the authority of Rab’i ibn Harash, on the authority of Imran ibn Husayn, on the authority of his father, that he came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted him and said: O Muhammad, Abdul Muttalib was better for your people than you. He used to feed them liver and hump, and you slaughtered them, so he said He said to him what God wanted him to say, then he said to him: “Say: O God, protect me from the evil of my soul, and guide me to the right path in my affairs.” He said: Then he came to him while he was a Muslim. He said: You told me what you said, so how do I say it now that I am a Muslim? He said: “Say: O God, forgive me for what I concealed and what I declared, what I erred and what I deliberately did, and what I was ignorant of.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10336","Zakaria bin Yahya told me, he said: Othman told us, he is Ibn Abi Shaybah, he said: Muhammad bin Bishr told us, he said: Zakaria told us He is Ibn Abi Zaida. He said: Mansour bin Al-Mu’tamir told us, he said: Rabi’ bin Harash told me, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, he said: Husayn came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, before he converted to Islam, and said: O Muhammad, Abdul-Muttalib was better for your people than you. He feeds them with liver and hump, and you slaughter them. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him, “What God wished for him to say.” Then, indeed, a strong man. He said: O Muhammad, what do you command me to say? He said: “You say: O God, I seek refuge in You from the evil of my soul, and I ask You to help me guide my affairs.” Then Husayn converted to Islam after that. He came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: I asked you the first time, and I am saying now: What do you command me to say? He said: “Say: O God, forgive me for what I have concealed and what I have declared, what I have done wrong and what I have been ignorant of, and what I have known.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10337","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Nufayl said: Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, conveyed the news, he would rhyme with a joke: And he will bring you news from someone who did not \provide\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"10338","Omar bin Muhammad bin Al-Hasan bin Al-Tall informed us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Awanah, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhajir, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Aisha She said: “Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sought out news, he would go to the house of Tarfa, and he would bring you news if you did not provide it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10339","Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: Sharik told us, on the authority of Al-Miqdam bin Shurayh, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, it was said to her: Was it Did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, imitate some poetry? She said: “He used to imitate the poetry of Ibn Rawaha: He would bring you news if you did not provide it.”"
"10340","Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala bin Abdul-Jabbar Al-Attar and Imran bin Yazid bin Abi Jamil Al-Dimashqi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Maysarah, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Sharid, on the authority of his father, said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, led me behind him, and said: “Do you have someone with you?” Umayyad poetry? “I said: Yes, he said: “Heh,” and Imran said: “Bring it.” So I recited a verse, and he kept saying: “Heh” until I recited it."
"10341","Harun bin Abdullah told us, he said: Maan told us, he said: Malik told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Khusayfa, on the authority of Amr bin Abd. Allah bin Ka'b, that Nafi' bin Jubayr told him, on the authority of Uthman bin Abi Al-Asi, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to me to return from The pain became severe in me, so he said: “Wipe with your right hand seven times and say: I seek refuge in God’s glory and power from the evil I am facing.” So I did, and God went away. Whatever happened to me, I continued to order it to my family and others."
"10342","Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: Ismail told us. Abu Salih Muhammad bin Zanbour al-Makki told us, saying: Ismail bin Ja`far told us, he said: Yazid bin Khusayfa told us, on the authority of Amr bin Abdullah bin Ka’b said that Nafi’ bin Jubayr told him that Uthman bin Abi Al-Asi came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He was seized with pain that almost paralyzed him, so he mentioned that to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he claimed that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He said: “Put your right hand on the place where you complain, wipe it seven times, and say: I seek refuge in the glory and power of God from the evil that I find in every “Anointing.” The pronunciation is by Abu Salih (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10343","Ahmad ibn Amr ibn al-Sarh informed us, he said: Ibn Wahb informed us, he said: Yunus informed us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: he informed me Nafi’ bin Jubayr, on the authority of Uthman bin Abi Al-Aas Al-Thaqafi, that he complained to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about a pain he found in his body. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “Put your hand on the part of your body that hurts and say: In the name of God three times, and say seven times: I seek refuge.” By God and His power, I seek protection from the evil of whatever I encounter.” Yasin bin Abdul-Ahad bin Al-Layth bin Asim told us, he said: My grandfather told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Al-Hakam, he said: Yunus told me, On the authority of Ibn Shihab, that Nafi’ bin Jubayr told him that Uthman bin Abi Al-Asi complained to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about a pain he was experiencing. The hadith was transmitted as mursal"
"10344","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ziyad bin Thuwaib, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came and then mentioned a word that means: He will return to me, so he said: “Shall I not perform ruqyah to you in the same way that Jibreel ruqyah did to me?” I said: Yes, may my mother and father be sacrificed. He said: “In the name of God, I recite ruqyah for you, and may God heal you from every disease in you, from the evil of blowing on the knot, and from the evil of the envier.” When he envied (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10345","Abu Asim Khushish bin Asram Al-Nasa’i told us, he said: ‘Arim told us, he said: Thabit, who is Ibn Yazid Abu Zaid, told us, he said: Asim told us, on the authority of Salman, a man from the Levant, on the authority of Junada, on the authority of Ibn al-Samit, who said: I entered upon the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, one morning. He was in pain, the severity of which God knows. Then I entered upon him in the evening and he had been healed. He said: “Gabriel gave me a telegram and I was healed. Will I not Shall I teach you that, O son of the silent one? “I said: Yes. He said: “In the name of God, I perform ruqyah for you, from everything that harms you, from the envy of every envious person and eye, in the name of God. \Heal you\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"10346","Bishr bin Hilal told us, he said: Abdul-Warith told us, on the authority of Abdul-Aziz bin Suhayb, on the authority of Abu Nadra, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, “Gabriel came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Muhammad, have you complained? He said: Yes. He said: In the name of God, I recite ruqyah for you, from all “Something that harms you, from the evil of every soul or envier, in the name of God I recite ruqyah for you, and God will heal you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10347","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Yazid told us, and Abu Amir told us, they said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Minhal, on the authority of Saeed Ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he used to seek refuge with Al-Hasan and Al-Husayn: “I seek refuge with you with the perfect words of God, from Every devil and wild beast, and from the evil of every eye is a nation.” And he says: “This is how my father Abraham used to protect Ishmael and Isaac.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10348","Muhammad ibn Qudamah told me, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Minhal ibn Amr, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to seek refuge with Hasan and Husayn: I seek refuge with you with the perfect words of God, from every devil and creature. And from every spring there is a blame.” And he used to say: “Your father used to seek refuge with him in Ishmael and Isaac.” Zakaria bin Yahya told us, he said: Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to seek refuge with Hasan and Husayn, on a mission. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10349","Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, “that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, Whenever he complained, he would recite the exorcists to himself and blow his nose. When his pain became severe, I would recite them to him and wipe his hand over him in hope. \Her blessing\"""""
"10350","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Sulayman told us, on the authority of Muslim, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to seek refuge with some of his family, wiping his hand, and saying: “O God, Lord of people, remove the violence.” “And heal, You are the Healer. There is no cure except Your cure, a cure that does not leave behind any disease.” Sufyan said: I told him Mansour, and he told me, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, something similar."
"10351","Muhammad bin Qudamah told me, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, she said: It was When the sick person came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he would pray for him: “Remove the affliction, Lord of the people, and heal, You are the healer. There is no cure except your recovery. A cure that does not leave behind a disease.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10352","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Abu Numan told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Stolen, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: Whenever a sick person was brought to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he would say: Remove the affliction, Lord of the people, and heal, You are the Healer. There is no cure except Your healing, a healing that leaves no disease behind.”"
"10353","Uqba bin Qabisah bin Uqba told us, he said: My father told me, he said: Warqa’ told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Stolen, on the authority of Aisha, that whenever the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, visited a sick person, he would say: “Remove the affliction, Lord of the people, and heal, You are the healer. There is no cure except your cure, a cure that does not leave any illness behind.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10354","Abdah bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, he said: Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Israel told us, and Ahmad bin Suleiman told us, And Al-Qasim bin Zakaria bin Dinar, they said: Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Mansur, on the authority of Ibrahim, and Muslim bin Subaih, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: Whenever the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, sought refuge with anyone, and Abdah said: Sick, he said: “Remove the affliction, Lord of the people, and heal you, you are the healer. There is no cure except your recovery, a cure that leaves no disease behind.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10355","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, he said: Khaled bin Nizar told us, he said: Nafi’ told us. Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Hakam informed us, saying: Al-Khasib ibn Nasih narrated to us, saying: Nafi’ ibn Umar narrated to us. Al-Jumahi, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika, on the authority of Aisha, who said: I used to wipe the chest of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with my hand, and Muhammad said: Ali The chest of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I say: “Remove the calamity, Lord of the people. You are the Physician and You are the Healer.” She said: And he says: Join me with the comrade, join me with the comrade.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10356","Imran bin Musa told us, he said: Abd al-Wahid bin Ziyad told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, he said: She said: Aisha, may God be pleased with her: “When one of his family complained, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to wipe him with his right hand: ‘Remove the violence. Lord of the people, heal you, you are the healer, there is no cure except your healing, a healing that does not leave behind an illness.”"
"10357","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Abdullah bin Wahb told us, he said: Dawud bin Abdul-Rahman told me, on the authority of Amr bin Yahya Al-Mazini, on the authority of Yusuf bin Muhammad bin Thabit bin Qais bin Shammas, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He entered upon him and said: “Remove the evil, Lord of the people,” on the authority of Thabit bin Qais bin Shammas, then he took dirt from Buthan and put it in a cup. There was water in it, so he poured it on him. Ibn Jurayj disagreed with him. Ali bin Sahl told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, Ibn Jurayj said: Amr bin Yahya bin Amara told us, he said: Yusuf told me Bin Muhammad bin Thabit bin Qais bin Shammas: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to Thabit bin Qais, sending (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10358","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, he said: Hisham bin Urwa told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, She said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to seek refuge, saying: “Wipe away the affliction, Lord of the people. There is no cure except your recovery. Heal with a cure that will not depart.” \sickness\"""""
"10359","Ali ibn Khashram informed us, he said: Jesus informed us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: He was the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He recited a ruqyah: “Eliminate the calamity, Lord of the people. In your hand is healing. There is no one to remove it except you.”"
"10360","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Muawiyah bin Salih told us, on the authority of Azhar bin Saeed, on the authority of Abdul Al-Rahman bin Al-Sa’ib bin my brother Maimunah, that Maimunah said to me: O son of my brother, should I not perform ruqyah for you according to the telegram of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? I said: Yes, she said: “In the name of God I perform incantation for you, and God will heal you from every disease that you have. Remove the affliction, Lord of the people, and heal, and you are the healer, there is no curer.” \Except you\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"10361","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abd al-Warith told us, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz bin Suhayb, he said: Thabit al-Bunani and I entered. On Anas bin Malik, and Thabit said: O Abu Hamza, I complained, so he said: Shall I not perform ruqyah for you according to the ruqyah of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? I said: Yes, he said: “O God, Lord of people, remove the affliction, heal You are the Healer, there is no healer but You, a cure that does not leave behind a disease.”"
"10362","Ubayd Allah ibn Sa`id Abu Qudamah al-Sarkhasi informed us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of `Abd Rabbuh, who is ibn Sa`id, on the authority of Amra, On the authority of Aisha, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to say to the sick person, “Thus spread his spit on the ground with his finger,” and he would say: “In the name of God, the soil of our land, the sparkling of some, through it our sick will be healed, with the permission of our Lord.” Abu Abd al-Rahman told us: We do not know of anyone who narrated this hadith except Ibn Uyaynah."
"10363","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Muhammad bin Hatib, he said: I ate a pot of Then some of its water got on my palm, and the back of my palm was burned, so my mother took me to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “Go away in valor, Lord of the people.” “And I think he said: “And heal, you are the one who heals,” and he spit. Zakariya bin Abi Zaida and Mis’ar disagreed with him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10364","Abdah bin Abdullah told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Bishr, he said: Zakaria bin Abi Zaida told us, on the authority of Simak bin Harb, on the authority of Muhammad bin Hatib said: I took a pot that was mine, and my hand was burned, so my mother took me to a sitting man, and said to him: O Messenger of God, He said: “By your service and my happiness.” Then she brought me closer to him, and he began to spit and speak words that I did not know what they were, so I asked my mother after that: What? Was he saying? She said: He used to say: “Remove the affliction, Lord of the people. Heal, You are the healer. There is no healer but You.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10365","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Ja’far bin Aoun told us, he said: Mas’ar said: He told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Muhammad bin Hatib, He said: My mother made broth and it spilled on my hands, so my mother took me to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said something that I did not remember, so I asked her. About him in the Emirate of Othman: What did he say? She said: He said: “Remove the suffering, Lord of the people, and heal, You are the healer.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10366","Ahmad bin Sulayman told us, he said: Ali told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Iyas, on the authority of Abu Nadra, on the authority of Abu Saeed, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent us thirty men, and we camped with a people at night, but they refused to host us, so we camped in a town. Then their master was stung, so they came to us and said: Is there anyone among you who performs ruqyah? We said: Yes. They said: So go. We said: No, unless you give us a sheep. You refused to host us. So they gave us thirty sheep, so I set off. with them, so I began to recite the Fatihah of the Book, and wipe the place that had been stung until it was healed, so they gave us the sheep, and I said: By God, we will not eat them. I do not know what ruqyah is, nor am I good at ruqyah. When we came to Medina, we came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we told him, and he said: “And what do you know? It is a ruqyah, and who taught you that it is a ruqyah? Yes, so eat it and strike an arrow for me with you."
"10367","Muhammad ibn Bashhar told us, he said: Muhammad told us, and he mentioned a word that means, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Abu Al-Mutawakkil, on the authority of Abu Saeed, that some of the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to an Arab neighborhood, but they did not approach them. While they were thus, the master of those was stung, and he said: Is there any medicine or potion among you? They said: You have not accepted us, so we will not do so until you make for us a flock. So they made for themselves a herd of sheep, and he began to recite the Mother of the Qur’an. He collected his sputum and exhaled, and the man was healed. They brought the thing and said: We will not take it until we ask the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So they asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he laughed and said: “How do you know that it is a ruqyah? Take it and hit me with an arrow in it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10368","Ziyad bin Ayyub Abu Hashim told me, his two dialects, he said: Hushaym told us, he said: Abu Bishr told us, on the authority of Abu al-Mutawakkil, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri said that some of the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, were on a journey and they passed through an Arab neighborhood. So they hosted them, but they refused to host them, so one of them was hurt in the mind or bitten, so they said to the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him He said: Is there a classy person among you? Then one of them said: Yes, I am. Then their companion came and separated him with the opening of the book, and he was healed. He was given a flock of sheep, but he refused. He accepted it until he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and mentioned that to him, so he said: O Messenger of God, by the One who sent you with the truth, I only promoted him. With the opening of the book, he laughed and said: “How do you know that it is a ruqyah?” Then he said: “Take the sheep and hit me with an arrow with you.” Ziyad bin Ayyub told me, he said: Abu Muawiyah, Ya’la, and Muhammad told us, they said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Iyas, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, on the authority of Abu Sa`id, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, similarly (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10369","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad Al-Zaafrani told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, he said: Ibn Jurayj told us, Amr bin Yahya told us, he said: Maryam told me Bint Iyas, on the authority of some of the wives of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Do you have any offspring?” and she said: Yes. So he called for it and put it on a blister between two of his toes, then he said: “O God, who extinguishes the great and magnifies the small. Turn it off from me.” So it turned off (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10370","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Muhammad bin Jaafar told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Al-Safar, on the authority of Al-Shu’abi, On the authority of Kharijah ibn al-Salt, on the authority of his uncle, he said: We came from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we came to a neighborhood of Arabs, and they said: Did Do you have any medicine or ruqyah? For with us is a fool in chains, so they brought a fool in chains, and I recited to him the Fatiha of the Book for three days, morning and evening. I collect my slugs. And he spit, as if he was more energetic than a camel. So they gave me a camel, and I said: No, and they said: Ask the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, so I asked him and he said: “Eat.” By my life, whoever eats a telegram of falsehood has eaten a telegram of truth.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10371","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, on the authority of Ammar bin Ruzaiq, on the authority of Abdullah bin Issa, on the authority of Umayyah Ibn Hind, he said: Abu Abdul Rahman told us this, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Amir Ibn Rabi’ah, on the authority of his father, he said: I went out Sahl bin Hunaif and I were looking for wine, so we poured a pool of wine. One of us was ashamed to be naked while someone could see him, so he covered himself until then. He saw that he had done so, and he took off a wool cloak over himself, and I liked his character, so I struck him with an evil eye, and a rattling took him over, so I called him, but he did not answer me. So I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and informed him, and he said: “Stand up with us.” Then he rose from his legs until the water ran towards him, and it was as if I were looking at He spread the legs of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he beat his chest and said: “In the name of God, O God, remove its heat and cold and pour water on it. Arise. God willing.” Then he stood up, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “If one of you sees something about himself, his property, or his brother that he likes, So let him pray for blessing, for the evil eye is true.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10372","Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Al-Mu’alla bin Asad told us, he said: Abdul-Wahid bin Ziyad told us, he said: Othman bin Hakim, he said: My grandmother Al-Rabbab told me, she said: I heard Sahl bin Hunaif, saying: We passed by a flood, so I bathed in it, and came out carried by it. He had a fever, so the matter reached the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “See Abu Thabit who is seeking refuge.” I said: Sir, is the ruqyah valid? He said: “There is no ruqyah except in the case of a sore throat, a fever, or a bite.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10373","Abd al-Hamid bin Muhammad told us, he said: Mukhlid told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Talq, on the authority of his father, that he was He was captured, so he went to Medina and the Levant, seeking someone to heal him. He met a man and said: Shall I not teach you some words I heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? May God bless him and grant him peace: “Our Lord, God who is in heaven, hallowed be your name. Your command is in heaven and earth. Just as I showed your mercy in heaven, make your mercy on earth. Forgive us our trespasses and our sins, You are the Lord of the good ones. Send down a mercy from Your mercy and a cure from Your healing upon this affliction and it will be healed.” Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: Abu Dawud told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: Yunus bin Khabab told me, he said: I heard Talaq bin Habib, on the authority of a man from the Levant, on the authority of his father, that a man came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he was captive, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, ordered him to May God bless him and grant him peace, to say: “Our Lord, God, whose name is sanctified in heaven,” and he cited the hadith. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10374","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Al-Layth told me, and another one before him mentioned, on the authority of Ziadah bin Muhammad, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ka’b al-Qurazi, on the authority of Abu al-Darda’, that a man came to him and mentioned that his father had retained his urine, so it infected him. Urinary stones, so he taught him a ruqyah that he heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Our Lord who is in heaven, hallowed be your name, your command in heaven And the earth, just as I showed Your mercy in the sky, so extend Your mercy to the earth, and forgive us our trespasses and our sins. You are the Lord of the good, so send down a cure for Your healing, and your mercy upon this pain, and he will be healed.” And he commanded him to perform ruqyah for him with it, so he performed ruqyah for him with it, and he was healed. Ibn Abi Maryam disagreed with him. Ahmad bin Saad bin Al-Hakam bin Abi Maryam told us, on the authority of his uncle, he said: Al-Layth narrated to me, he said: Ziyadah bin Muhammad narrated to me Al-Ansari, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ka’b, on the authority of Fadalah, said: Two men from the people of Iraq came seeking recovery for their father who had withheld his urine, so he comforted him. The people came to Abu Darda, and the two men came to him with some leftovers. They mentioned to him, and Abu Darda said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He says: “Whoever complains about something among you, or a brother of his complains, let him say so.” So he mentioned something similar to it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10375","Siwar bin Abdullah bin Siwar told us, he said: Abdul Wahhab bin Abdul Majeed told us, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered upon a Bedouin who was visiting him, and said: “There is nothing wrong with you, you will be pure, God willing.” He said: No, but rather Say: A fever bubbling in the bones of an old man, as if graves visit him. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “So yes, then.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10376","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Dawud bin Abdul-Rahman told me, on the authority of Amr bin Yahya. Al-Mazni, on the authority of Yusuf bin Muhammad bin Thabit bin Qais bin Shammas, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that He entered upon him and said: “Remove the calamity, Lord of mankind, on the authority of Thabit bin Qais bin Shamas.” Then he took some dirt from Buthan and put it in a cup of water. So he poured it on him. Ibn Jurayj disagreed with him. Ali bin Sahl told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, Ibn Jurayj said: Amr bin Yahya bin Amara told me, he said: Yusuf told me Bin Muhammad bin Thabit bin Qais bin Shammas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to Thabit bin Qais, and likewise, on a mission. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10377","Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Affan told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Humayd, and Hammad, on the authority of Anas: that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace. Whenever he visited a sick person, he would say: “Remove the affliction, O Lord of people, and heal You who are the healer, a cure that leaves no ailment behind.” And Hammad said: “No.” There is no cure except your recovery. Heal a cure that does not leave behind a disease.”"
"10378","Wahb bin Bayan told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Amr bin Al-Harith told me, on the authority of Abd Rabbuh bin Saeed, he said Al-Minhal bin Amr told me, and once Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace When the sick person returned, he, peace and blessings be upon him, sat at his head, then said seven times: “I ask God Almighty, Lord of the Magnificent Throne, to heal you. If there is a delay in its term, then he will be relieved of that pain.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10379","Al-Hasan bin Ismail bin Sulayman Al-Mujalidi told me, he said: Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Minhal, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Al-Harith, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “No Muslim enters upon a sick person who has not attended his appointment.” Then he says: I ask God Almighty, Lord of the Great Throne, to heal you seven times, unless God heals you.”"
"10380","Ahmad bin Ibrahim told me, he said: Abu Al-Nadr told us, he said: Muhammad bin Shuaib told us, he said: Shu’bah bin Al-Hajjaj told me, On the authority of Maysarah, on the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “ If one of you visits a sick person whose death has not come, and says: I ask God Almighty, Lord of the Mighty Throne, to heal you seven times, God will heal you.” Abdul-Samad bin Abdul-Wahhab told us, he said: Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Muhammad bin Shuaib told us, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of Maysara, on the authority of al-Manhaal, the same is the same, and he did not say “seven times.” Zakaria bin Yahya told us, he said: Abu Bakr Al-Adhrami told me, he said: Ahmad bin Humayd told us, he said: Al-Ashja’i told me, On the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Maysarah, on the authority of Al-Minhal, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: So he mentioned Towards him (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10381","Amr bin Ali and Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, saying: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Yazid, he said: I heard al-Minhaal Ibn Amr narrates, on the authority of Saeed Ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “No Muslim servant visits a sick person.” His time has not come, so he says seven times: I ask God Almighty, Lord of the Magnificent Throne, to heal you, unless He is a pardoner.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10382","Ishaq bin Ibrahim informed us, he said: Sufyan informed us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Let none of you say: I have licked myself.”"
"10383","Muhammad bin Hisham Al-Sadusi informed us, saying: Omar bin Ali told us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Hussein, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, She said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Let none of you say: I have licked myself.” Yunus and Ishaq bin Rashid disagreed with him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10384","Wahb bin Bayan told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Yunus told us, he said: Muhammad bin Yahya bin Kathir told us Al-Harrani, he said: Muhammad bin Musa told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Ishaq bin Rashid, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Umamah bin Sahl, On the authority of his father, the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Let none of you say: My soul has been corrupted, but let him say: I have licked myself.” The word “wahb” means “wahb.” Sufyan disagreed with them (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10385","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Umamah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Let none of you say: I am an evil person, but let him say: I am a licentious person.”"
"10386","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, saying: Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Humayd. And Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Khaled bin Al-Harith told us, he said: Humaid told us, on the authority of Anas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, returned He, peace and blessings be upon him, greeted a man who had become like a chick, and said to him: “Have you been calling for something, or asking him about it?” He said: I was saying: Oh God, what You were punishing me with it in the Hereafter, so hasten it for me in this world. He said: “Glory be to God. You cannot or cannot bear it. Have you not said: Our Lord, give us in this world.” good, and good in the Hereafter, and protect us from the torment of the Fire.” In the hadith of Qutaibah, he said: So he prayed to God and He healed him. The wording is by Ibn al-Muthanna. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10387","Amr bin Ali told us, on the authority of Abu Dawud, he said: Shu`bah told us, he said: I heard Thabit, he said: I heard Anas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, often supplicates: “Our Lord, give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter, and protect us from the torment of the Fire.” Shu’bah said: So I mentioned That was for Qatada, and he said: Anas used to pray with this."
"10388","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Salim bin Nuh told us, Saeed bin Abi Arouba said, Qatada told us, on the authority of Anas, that the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He went to see a man who was visiting him, and behold, it was as if he were a goat. The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to him: “Have you asked your Lord about Anything? This world is good, and the Hereafter is good.” The man said it, and he was pardoned. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10389","Ziyad bin Ayyub told us, he said: Ismail told us, he said: Abd al-Aziz told us, he said: Qatada asked Anas: What kind of invitation was it? What did the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, pray for most? He said: He used to supplicate the most, saying: “O God, give us good in this world, and good in the Hereafter, and protect us from the torment of the Fire.” And Anas was If he wanted to say a supplication, he would say it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10390","Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Anas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: None of you should wish for death because of harm that has befallen him. If he must wish for death, let him say: O God, grant me life as long as life is better for me, and cause me to die. If death is better for me.”"
"10391","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Salamah talking, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by me and I was saying: O God, if my time has come, then grant me relief. He was late, so comfort me, and if it was a calamity, then be patient with me. Then he hit me with his foot and said: “O God, heal him, O God, heal him,” and I did not complain of my pain. That's after"
"10392","Muhammad bin Bashar informed us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz bin Suhayb, that he heard Anas bin Malik narrated, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “None of you should wish for death because of harm that has befallen him. If he must do something, let him say: Oh God, keep me alive as long as life is good for me, and cause me to die if death is good for me.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10393","Abdullah bin Al-Haytham bin Othman told us, he said: Abu Dawud told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Qatada, he said: he told us Anas: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The believer should not wish to die as a result of harm that befell him. If he must do something, let him say: Oh God.” “Give me life as long as life is good for me, and grant me death as long as death is good for me.”"
"10394","10405 Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Al-Nadr told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: Ali bin Zaid told me, he said: I heard Anas bin Malik said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “None of you should wish for death, or he said: The believer is death, if it is necessary.” So let him say: O God, keep me alive as long as life is good for me, and cause me to die if death is good for me.”"
"10395","Harun bin Abdullah told me, he said: Sayyar told us, he said: Ja`far told us, he said: Thabit told us, on the authority of Anas, he said: He entered The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came upon Thabit while he was dying, and he said to him: “How do you find yourself?” He said: I hope in God, O Messenger of God, and I fear. My sins, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The two do not come together in the heart of a servant in such a place except that God gives him what he hopes for. And made him safe from what he feared.”"
